From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:13:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 154/155] kk: MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault logs a failed command
 buffer's encoders

A Metal command buffer that fails loses the device for good, and the
driver logged only the localized description of the commit feedback's
error ("MTL4CommandQueueErrorDomain error 1", which the SDK's
MTL4CommandQueueError names Timeout: the workload took longer than the
system allows). Metal 4 has no public encoder execution status:
MTL4CommitFeedback gives an NSError and two GPU times, and
MTL4CommandBufferOptions has only a log state.

Always, a failed commit now also logs ([kk-queue] error:) the whole
error chain, a line per item: domain, code, description and failure
reason, every user info entry, Metal's encoder infos
(MTLCommandBufferEncoderInfoErrorKey: label, state, signposts) and the
underlying errors (NSUnderlyingErrorKey, NSMultipleUnderlyingErrorsKey)
in turn, then the feedback object's class and methods; and its timing
(commit to GPU start, GPU run, GPU end to feedback). An error code the
enum lacks maps to a name instead of being unreachable.

With MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault (kk_fault.h):
- every encoder is labelled "kk#<cb serial>.<index> render draws=N" or
  "... compute dispatches=N copies=N", with tess, gs, unroll, heap and
  indirect when it did them;
- each recording keeps that trail; a failed commit logs it ([kk-fault]
  cb #N failed ..., one line per encoder) with the serial of the last
  command buffer that completed;
- each reset of the 128 MiB geometry heap that tessellation, geometry
  shaders and strip unrolls allocate from first copies the bytes the
  previous user allocated into a ring; a failure logs the heap's
  header and the ring's largest entry, and a completed command buffer
  that used the heap logs each new high-water mark (first, then 8 MiB
  more, or an overflow);
- device creation logs whether the runtime's MTL4CommandBufferOptions
  answers to setErrorOptions: (then every command buffer begins with
  encoder execution status asked for) and the methods of the commit
  and command buffer option classes.

Without the flag no encoder is labelled and nothing is recorded.

Linear: PLA-880
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: build/mesa-host-test/kk-fault-test.c (mock Metal, a failed commit's lines); PLA-880 (13 of 18 The Witcher 3 1.32 loads lost the device on one failed command buffer)
Offered-upstream: no
